# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { ref } from 'vue'

export default {
	setup() {
		const count = ref(0)
		const value = count.value
		return { value }
	}
}

function useCounter() {
	const count = ref(0)
	console.log(count.value)
	return count
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-setup.js:7:17 lint/nursery/noVueRefObjectReactivityLoss ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This reads the value of a ref only once, so it won't update when the ref changes.
  
    5 │ 	setup() {
    6 │ 		const count = ref(0)
  > 7 │ 		const value = count.value
      │ 		              ^^^^^^^^^^^
    8 │ 		return { value }
    9 │ 	}
  
  i This code runs only once, together with the code that creates the ref. The value read here is a copy, and Vue does not update it when the ref changes.
  
  i Read .value inside a function, such as a computed() getter, or pass the ref itself instead of its value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

